{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1413224-what-is-ventru-doing-what\u2019s-his-deal","id":1413224,"title":"What is Ventru doing? What\u2019s his deal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-12T07:11:09-07:00","id":1413224,"title":"What is Ventru doing? What\u2019s his deal?","content":"Like theirs barely any info on him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T07:56:00-07:00","id":1413229,"title":"","content":"What is he doing? What is his deal?<br /> <br /> &quot;Being dead&quot; is the answer to both.<br /> <br /> Most of the lore states Ventrue died shortly after the fall of the Second City, with only a few errors suggesting otherwise (such as sorting out who the Sire of Mithras), or other minor bits of business stating Ventrue survived by wants nothing to do with the jyhad (the non-canon Gehenna book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-12T08:02:19-07:00","id":1413230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1413224-what-is-ventru-doing-what\u2019s-his-deal#post1413224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like theirs barely any info on him</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ventrue antediluvian might be dead or in torpor somewhere. Asked on a forum 20 years ago about his status during Gehenna (which is obvioulsy not canon in the current metaplot) Justin Achilli (whose favourite clan were the Ventrue) suggested the Ventrue ante used Fortitude 10 to wait for Gehenna to be over avoiding the Jhyad and surviving it that way.<br /> <br /> Anyway the answer to your question, as with 99% of questions about antediluvians is: <b>you've got to decide about his status in your chronicle</b>.<br /> <br /> Edit: note that there's basically no info on a lot of antediluvians while others got chronicles dealing with them. The antediluvians of the Ventrue, Brujah (or Troile), Toreador, Gangrel, Assamite have very little information about them. We know a bit more about the Nosferatu, Malkavian, Setite and Lasombra antes. We know more about the Ravnos ante. We know the most about the Salubri (and Tremere), Tzimisce and Cappadocian (or Giovanni) antes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 09-12-2020, 11:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T08:21:30-07:00","id":1413375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1413224-what-is-ventru-doing-what\u2019s-his-deal?p=1413229#post1413229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is he doing? What is his deal?<br /> <br /> &quot;Being dead&quot; is the answer to both.<br /> <br /> Most of the lore states Ventrue died shortly after the fall of the Second City, with only a few errors suggesting otherwise (such as sorting out who the Sire of Mithras), or other minor bits of business stating Ventrue survived by wants nothing to do with the jyhad (the non-canon Gehenna book).</div> </div> </div> </div>That, and there being a lot of 4th-Gen Ventrue around whose lore doesn't suggest they were sired during the Second City (Antonius, Erik and so forth).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T08:41:00-07:00","id":1413380,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think Ventrue/Veddartha is dead. There are too many Fourth Gen Ventrue Sired long after the Second City (Mithras is only the most famous).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T09:31:51-07:00","id":1413385,"title":"","content":"As for how a large number of Ventrue might be 4th generation without Ventrue/Veddartha....<br /> ...Diablerie is a hell of a drug. And so is lying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T10:31:43-07:00","id":1413393,"title":"","content":"I have always pictured a very weird, totally different answer, that combines a lot of the previous theories. Venture let his physical form be destroyed, so he could become a &quot;god&quot;/High Umbra spirit. However, he saved numerous vials of his Vitae before this happened. He then had chosen servants (ghouls, a favored Childe, or something else) use a vial to Sire new Childer. A different servant could embrace each one, giving a different name or at least an identity to each.This would explain why the Clan thinks him destroyed, how there could be so many embraced after his 'death,' how each one knows a different name, etc. The 'blood god' Ventrue could then keep contact with the very special childer via Auspex or some other means, leading to the possibility of a second group of beings taking charge of the world. I know it is out there, but it does connect a lot of the dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T12:11:06-07:00","id":1413410,"title":"","content":"Probably still alive. I dont think he is Veddartha. The sire of Mithras is a 4th gen member of the inconnu as far as i am concerned. I think the original idea was that he died a long time ago. But his death would contradict canon. A lot of 4th gen ventrue's were made long time after his supposed demise. So they retconned it..The beckoning proves this (unless you believe the antes arent behind the beckoning).The only elders that arent being called, are members of the hecata. So Cappa might be the only dead ante. Even ravnos could still be out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 09-13-2020, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T12:23:21-07:00","id":1413417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1413224-what-is-ventru-doing-what\u2019s-his-deal?p=1413393#post1413393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always pictured a very weird, totally different answer, that combines a lot of the previous theories. Venture let his physical form be destroyed, so he could become a &quot;god&quot;/High Umbra spirit. However, he saved numerous vials of his Vitae before this happened. He then had chosen servants (ghouls, a favored Childe, or something else) use a vial to Sire new Childer. A different servant could embrace each one, giving a different name or at least an identity to each.This would explain why the Clan thinks him destroyed, how there could be so many embraced after his 'death,' how each one knows a different name, etc. The 'blood god' Ventrue could then keep contact with the very special childer via Auspex or some other means, leading to the possibility of a second group of beings taking charge of the world. I know it is out there, but it does connect a lot of the dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be it.<br /> Another related idea: maybe Ventrue's Dominate 10 power allows him to temporarily grant his generation to whichever vampire he possesses. So most of the time he's a spirit, but when he wants to pop out a baby 4rth gen, he possesses one of his childer, boosts their gen while he's in them, embraces someone, and then leaves them as soon as he's trained his baby 4rth gen in whatever its duties are to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T18:48:46-07:00","id":1413470,"title":"","content":"His most trusted childe can be Balthazar so i'd point his location somewhere between modern day Iran and Tajikistan. He traveled as far as to Athens when he embraced Alexander in 700 BC or Gaul for Antonius in 500 BC and got to Rome after its fall in the 6th century to embrace Maltheas, that's his last recorded entry (perhaps only known to the roman Inconnu).<br /> <br /> I'd like to believe that the Beckoning was partially on his behalf.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T18:59:44-07:00","id":1413475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1413224-what-is-ventru-doing-what\u2019s-his-deal?p=1413470#post1413470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His most trusted childe can be Balthazar so i'd point his location somewhere between modern day Iran and Tajikistan. He traveled as far as to Athens when he embraced Alexander in 700 BC or Gaul for Antonius in 500 BC and got to Rome after its fall in the 6th century to embrace Maltheas, that's his last recorded entry (perhaps only known to the roman Inconnu).<br /> <br /> I'd like to believe that the Beckoning was partially on his behalf.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, that timeline actually makes sense. Are you certain that Mithras is not his Childe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T20:14:02-07:00","id":1413482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1413224-what-is-ventru-doing-what\u2019s-his-deal?p=1413475#post1413475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, that timeline actually makes sense. Are you certain that Mithras is not his Childe?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't mention Mithras because I'd already assumed he was his childe <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T20:47:13-07:00","id":1413485,"title":"","content":"Perfect! Thanks \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T22:37:59-07:00","id":1413495,"title":"","content":"I have Ventrue be one of the real dead ones (Brujah being the second, and a few who were slain so early the never created clans). I always liked the idea of the clan being without an ante. I have it as their original reasoning why they should lead. Because they are not influenced by a blood god of old times. Which they forgot over time and now are simply stating they are none existent.<br /> <br /> I have Veddertha holding the remnants together after Ventrues death. Starting the tradition with finding a nice weakened 4th gen of another clan to thicken the blood if a childe showed the right potential. Might makes indeed right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T09:44:05-07:00","id":1413574,"title":"","content":"I imagine a few cirucumstances in regard to the Ventrue Founder. Of course he is well and active (if such a simple distinction could be said to describe him and what he does). He stays at the most expensive and luxurious apartments and hotels there can be, close to city centers, airports and major train stations ; changing them as his moods and plans change. At any place he stays for a longer time, he manipulates, coaxes, or orders Ventrue Vampires, Ghouls and Blood Bound servants into securing a particular location for him. So lobbies of hotels and nearby high class restaurants are filled with Ghouls and Blood Bound servants, while the rented conference rooms and private suites host meetings (social or otherwise) of Ventrue Vampires. It has to be noted just how much Presence and Dominate helps with this kind of arranging.<br /> He pretends to be a Methuselah pretending to be a Vampire Elder, and thus a Vampire who manages to penetrate enough of his buffer zone might even get a glimpse of him. A conversation, a few words, an item or a message given ; most often through intermediaries but sometimes personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-14-2020, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T20:34:55-07:00","id":1413897,"title":"","content":"You know, it's at least possible [Ventrue] is in torpor somewhere because of her feeding restrictions. Maybe it was &quot;humans from the Second City&quot;.<br /> <br /> And over the years, now and again, particular mortals stumble upon her form, are overwhelmed by her sheer mental prowess, drain themselves dry, drink a droplet of her blood, and thus become agents to the slumbering ancient who doesn't even notice she keeps spawning 4th Generation vampires.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T12:47:53-07:00","id":1414018,"title":"","content":"I still maintain that for high level supernaturals 'death' has all the relevance it does in comic books. Deaths occur if convenient but they may not be permanent. And high level vampires (like many high level supernaturals) have ways to get around death in some way or another (what the cost may be is another matter.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-16T14:05:48-07:00","id":1414042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1413224-what-is-ventru-doing-what\u2019s-his-deal?p=1413897#post1413897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, it's at least possible [Ventrue] is in torpor somewhere because of her feeding restrictions. Maybe it was &amp;quot;humans from the Second City&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point the Ventrue weakness would be nullified by the methuselah's thirst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-18T11:07:12-07:00","id":1414426,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of [Ventrue] having died ages ago, but instead of cursing their clan to destruction like the Ravnos, they released their power and something of their spirit into the clan at large to carry on their legacy. Hence rather than falling apart the clan developed a culture of cooperation that's allowed them to hold so much more extensive domain/praxis than the others. And occasionally that shared power concentrates enough that a 4th generation vampire sires <i>another</i> 4th generation childe instead of the expected 5th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T11:35:16-07:00","id":1415708,"title":"","content":"My personal head canon regarding Ventru is that they continue to be the architect of their clan to these very nights.<br /> <br /> I imagine that their feeding restriction was that of the First City and that since the Deluge they have been slowly starving, falling to torpor, and briefly rising from time to time as the movements of fate allow.<br /> <br /> The Clan is aware of their antediluvian\u2019s activity through rumor and suspicion alone and their is a reason why elder Ventrue live in paranoia of secret masters guiding the great conspiracy of lords throughout the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T22:46:49-07:00","id":1415783,"title":"","content":"My non-canon take is that Ventrue is he's the original Antediluvian sire of Troile and thus the Modern Brujah are descendants of her after she diablerized him.<br /> <br /> Thus the irony of True Brujah is they're vampires trying to be more like Ventrue.<br /> <br /> I eventually went with something different and in my current game, Mithras killed the Ventrue Antediluvian (who had the symbol of a bull). So Ventrue has been dead for 6000 or so years.<br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue's Heirs</b><br /> <br /> Recently, I admit to having gone full comic book by having a 4th generation Ventrue escape the Beckoning and return to the Camarilla before declaring himself Primus (a title that never existed before) as well as Clan Leader. I'm pretty much going with the view that he's Vandal Savage in most respects because I'm terminally addicted to melodrama with my undead. The player characters are debating whether he's the actual Ventrue or just one of his oldest childer. If they ever talk with my 10,000 year old Ventrue, he'll basically just lay into the Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> &quot;You want to know what Ventrue built? A city of 5,000 people with huts of mud and clay! Everything this clan was built from was built from us! Just because he's old didn't make him a genius or a god! He was such an incompetent that he was the first king to ever have a revolt!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 09-28-2020, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}